data: {"type":"TOOL_CALL_RESULT","toolCallId":"call_00_4AcAXdI3ZY4xZKXiV6Dw8643","messageId":"c4e31d1c-cbc8-46ae-b9d6-1dbe19119867","content":"{\"ok\":true,\"result\":{\"path\":\"/skills/ui-plugin-development/SKILL.md\",\"content\":\"1: ---\\n2: name: ui-plugin-development\\n3: description: Edit project-owned UI Plugin code directly. Ask only before creating a new Plugin identity or first taking over an npm implementation.\\n4: compatibility: Agent UI Plugin Creator Phase 8 permits writes under project plugins and AppUIModel composition.\\n5: ---\\n6: \\n7: # UI Plugin development\\n8: \\n9: This Skill applies to frontend Plugin source/application authoring. The system\\n10: prompt owns general evidence, authorization and completion rules; this Skill\\n11: adds Plugin-specific contracts, not an additional investigation checklist.\\n12: Use the smallest relevant section/reference. A resolved existing target does not\\n13: require a full capability inventory, a new UI-system decision or a nearest\\n14: consumer example before it can be modified.\\n15: \\n16: ## Ownership and admission\\n17: \\n18: Project-owned application props, children, renderers and scoped styles are ordinary\\n19: editable code. Inspect the exact target and any concrete unknown contract; edit\\n20: within the user's request. Public npm component use does not require implementation\\n21: source, extraction or takeover. Existing source-owned Plugin edits keep the current\\n22: ownership, upstream provenance and BASE; do not repeat successful takeover consent.\\n23: Only actual npm implementation edits require `takeover_plugin_source` and its\\n24: explicit user agreement. Canonical Runtime/Context, vendor and generated registries\\n25: remain protected. A thin wrapper's omitted public seam is not justification for\\n26: requiring takeover.\\n27: \\n28: Ask `prepare_ui_plugin_development` once before creating a NEW Plugin identity,\\n29: including wrapping a component as a new Plugin. After confirmation, implement\\n30: its source, supporting modules, existing parent changes, composition and tests.\\n31: The question result is not a per-file allowlist; changed implementation details\\n32: never require the same development question again. Existing Plugin behavior,\\n33: new interactions and project Service files are ordinary edits. Only actual npm\\n34: implementation changes need the separate source-takeover question.\\n35: For new Plugin manifest/placement and delivery details consult only relevant\\n36: sections of [authoring contracts](references/authoring-contracts.md).\\n37: \\n38: ## Local change evidence\\n39: \\n40: Read the existing files that will change, using the actual supplied sourceRoot and\\n41: owner paths. `manifest.json` declares identity/data/capabilities; `definition.ts`\\n42: joins manifest and component; `index.tsx` owns composition/behavior; imported\\n43: stylesheets own presentation. Read a neighboring consumer only for wiring that\\n44: is actually unknown. An npm implementation need not appear in local search.\\n45: \\n46: `inspect_ui_plugin` returns application ownership, public APIs and parent semantic\\n47: composition where declared. sharedModule selects the installed public module;\\n48: use the root module for presentation controls and /contracts for Plugin types.\\n49: Use returned parameterContracts; follow exact parameterQueries only when a required\\n50: signature is missing. `$element` accesses an array/index element, not React props.\\n51: An unavailable guessed symbol is not a missing capability. Preserve declared\\n52: composition slots when appending controls; replacement props can replace them.\\n53: \\n54: Public types establish invocation shape, not rendered styling. Package-owned\\n55: presentationContract describes raw versus styled components, asset requirements\\n56: and Portal ownership. For a visual defect follow the current owned entry's CSS\\n57: imports and inspect the relevant cascade. Re-querying types cannot establish\\n58: centering. Public overlay composites may own their own Portal and Backdrop;\\n59: respect that composition and retain the existing AgentUIRoot theme container.\\n60: Use the public Trigger/Close/focus APIs. Local dialog state or scoped popup\\n61: positioning does not introduce a Service, Agent action, Runtime replacement or\\n62: source takeover. Verify requested placement, closing and focus in the actual Host.\\n63: \\n64: ## Editing constraints\\n65: \\n66: Freshly read existing edit targets in the current run; old messages/handoff are\\n67: navigation, not current read evidence. `edit_file_from_read` edits a stable range;\\n68: `edit_file` handles small local changes; `mutate_ui_plugin_source` makes one atomic\\n69: Plugin-local transaction with edit/create entries. Re-read and reconcile affected\\n70: files after stale-content errors. Do not hand-edit `registry.generated.ts`, the\\n71: AppUIModel JSON or composition-revision metadata; use their Host tools.\\n72: \\n73: Preserve the target's UI library, enabled capabilities, scope bridge, semantic\\n74: slots and original approval/interrupt/error renderers. New user/screen-reader copy\\n75: uses the unified domain locale namespace with en-US/zh-CN parity; never patch\\n76: vendor for localization. Read locale targets when changing them, not for every\\n77: style edit. Do not invent new per-Plugin i18n or Service abstractions.\\n78: \\n79: Styles must be imported and scoped to owned classes/data attributes; no global\\n80: resets, Host ancestor selectors, Runtime/Portal changes or vendor overrides.\\n81: Own box-sizing, min-width and responsive maximum size. Flex/grid children must\\n82: shrink and long text wrap; overlays need bounded dimensions appropriate to the\\n83: actual container. Static heuristics are not visual acceptance. The specialized\\n84: responsive-repair proposal tool is not currently exposed by any Creator tool\\n85: group. For ordinary authorized responsive CSS changes, freshly read the owned\\n86: stylesheet, use the available file-edit tools and validate the current revision.\\n87: If the user explicitly requests the unavailable specialized proposal tool,\\n88: explain that limitation; do not claim to have invoked it.\\n89: \\n90: ## Validation and outcome\\n91: \\n92: Validate source changes at the current revision; include the build for new visual\\n93: Plugins or dependency/style integration as required. Composition changes use fresh\\n94: AppUIModel evidence and normal Host mutation/verification tools. Creation/catalog\\n95: synchronization is not mounting: newly created capabilities must be composed when\\n96: requested, and the final revision validated. Consume checks already performed by\\n97: the Host rather than duplicating them. Respect returned repair limits.\\n98: \\n99: Keep static, Runtime and browser evidence distinct. Current tests/types or empty\\n100: Runtime errors do not prove popup geometry, keyboard behavior or focus. Validate\\n101: the requested interactions using available authorized browser/test evidence; report\\n102: missing infrastructure or stale evidence precisely. Do not label incomplete work\\n103: as already satisfied or reopen unrelated discovery when verification is unavailable.\\n104: \",\"hash\":\"d16638fb9d258001f57838e0d1ed8825997e8f323dc570b4ef1990f589272da5\",\"totalLines\":104,\"nextOffset\":null}}","role":"tool"}

data: {"type":"TOOL_CALL_START","toolCallId":"call_00_UVM7MgQCksgnbsuMr8oU6485","toolCallName":"read_file"}

data: {"type":"TOOL_CALL_ARGS","toolCallId":"call_00_UVM7MgQCksgnbsuMr8oU6485","delta":"{\"file_path\":\"/skills/ui-plugin-development/references/authoring-contracts.md\",\"limit\":160,\"offset\":0}"}

